c/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133456654,imgsize-1559771.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Massachusetts crew lands 1,260-pound blue marlin, misses world record]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133454734.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a thrilling encounter off Cape Cod, a charter captain teamed up with an angler to reel in an astonishing blue marlin that tipped the scales at 1,260 pounds and stretched over eleven feet. This remarkable catch approached the Atlantic blue marlin world record from 1992, prompting researchers to investigate its head to gauge its age. After the impressive capture, the fish was generously shared among several admirers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/massachusetts-fishing-crew-lands-1260-pound-blue-marlin-narrowly-missing-world-record/articleshow/133454734.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/massachusetts-fishing-crew-lands-1260-pound-blue-marlin-narrowly-missing-world-record/articleshow/133454734.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T13:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133455251,imgsize-1324041.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Four medaka fish flew into space in 1994; 43 eggs were laid and eight baby fish hatched]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133453313.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Astronaut Chiaki Mukai took four medaka fish into space in July 1994 as part of an experiment to study reproduction in microgravity. The fish laid eggs during the mission, with eight of 43 identified eggs hatching in space. After returning to Earth, the adult fish gradually recovered, while the young “space medaka” continued to grow normally.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/four-medaka-fish-flew-aboard-columbia-in-1994-to-test-whether-vertebrates-could-reproduce-without-gravity-they-laid-43-eggs-and-eight-baby-fish-hatched-in-space/articleshow/133453313.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/four-medaka-fish-flew-aboard-columbia-in-1994-to-test-whether-vertebrates-could-reproduce-without-gravity-they-laid-43-eggs-and-eight-baby-fish-hatched-in-space/articleshow/133453313.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133454480,imgsize-70899.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida turns 324-foot tanker into an underwater casino reef]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133454072.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-sank-a-324-foot-former-new-york-sludge-tanker-off-pompano-beach-the-wreck-became-an-underwater-casino-reef-with-card-dealing-sharks-poker-tables-and-marine-life/articleshow/133454072.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-sank-a-324-foot-former-new-york-sludge-tanker-off-pompano-beach-the-wreck-became-an-underwater-casino-reef-with-card-dealing-sharks-poker-tables-and-marine-life/articleshow/133454072.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T13:02:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133454294,imgsize-154634.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ohio home built entirely underground hits the market for $850,000 with a grass-covered roof]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133454771.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/this-ohio-home-built-entirely-underground-hits-the-market-for-850000-with-a-grass-covered-roof-that-the-owners-literally-have-to-mow/articleshow/133454771.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/this-ohio-home-built-entirely-underground-hits-the-market-for-850000-with-a-grass-covered-roof-that-the-owners-literally-have-to-mow/articleshow/133454771.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T12:39:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133455177,imgsize-1958403.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US sailor’s father detained by ICE while son serves aboard USS Abraham Lincoln]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133453708.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A US sailor's father, originally from Nicaragua, faced immigration officials' detention during a routine vehicle stop in Key West, Florida. While his son serves overseas, he feels deep concern for his father's situation, who is currently waiting for green card approval and possesses identification. This incident has raised eyebrows amid heightened scrutiny surrounding the USS Abraham Lincoln's prolonged deployment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-sailors-father-detained-by-ice-while-son-serves-aboard-uss-abraham-lincoln/articleshow/133453708.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-sailors-father-detained-by-ice-while-son-serves-aboard-uss-abraham-lincoln/articleshow/133453708.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T12:25:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133454659,imgsize-142122.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Washington releases 20 lab-raised sunflower stars to restore kelp forests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133454146.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable conservation initiative, twenty lab-raised sunflower sea stars have been released back into the Salish Sea. This effort seeks to restore a species that has suffered extensively due to disease, crucial for the health of kelp forest ecosystems. The project, undertaken in collaboration with the Samish Indian Nation and various researchers, symbolizes hope for restoring ecological balance in the region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/washington-releases-20-lab-raised-sunflower-sea-stars-into-the-salish-sea-to-restore-the-endangered-species-and-damaged-kelp-forests/articleshow/133454146.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/washington-releases-20-lab-raised-sunflower-sea-stars-into-the-salish-sea-to-restore-the-endangered-species-and-damaged-kelp-forests/articleshow/133454146.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T12:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133454416,imgsize-221584.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mexico brings back bison 160 years after extinction; 47 animals are restoring the ecosystem]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133453681.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After an absence of 160 years, American bison have made a remarkable comeback to Coahuila, Mexico. These majestic animals have become vital ecosystem engineers, actively rejuvenating worn-out landscapes. Their presence enhances soil quality and promotes water absorption in the dry terrain. Additionally, this return facilitates the resurgence of native predators and other wildlife, reflecting a wider initiative aimed at restoring vital species throughout North America.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/american-bison-had-been-hunted-to-extinction-in-mexico-160-years-later-the-country-introduced-47-bison-in-2025-and-the-ecosystem-is-slowly-restoring-itself/articleshow/133453681.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/american-bison-had-been-hunted-to-extinction-in-mexico-160-years-later-the-country-introduced-47-bison-in-2025-and-the-ecosystem-is-slowly-restoring-itself/articleshow/133453681.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T12:03:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133453766,imgsize-136470.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chinese humanoid robots beat Usain Bolt’s 100m record and human high-jump record: Are humans losing?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133451720.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At the recent Beijing Robot Games, humanoid robots set remarkable new benchmarks in speed and agility. One robot sprinted 100 meters in an astonishing 9.39 seconds, shattering Usain Bolt's record. Another demonstrated incredible prowess with a standing high jump of 2.88 meters, surpassing human limits. These milestones reflect China's advancements in the robotics field, yet experts caution that widespread adoption remains a future prospect.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/chinese-humanoid-robots-just-beat-usain-bolts-100m-record-and-the-human-high-jump-record-are-humans-already-losing-to-machines/articleshow/133451720.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/chinese-humanoid-robots-just-beat-usain-bolts-100m-record-and-the-human-high-jump-record-are-humans-already-losing-to-machines/articleshow/133451720.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133451830,imgsize-95897.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scotland recycles 72,000 contaminated single-use plastic bottles in a world-first move]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133452452.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scotland-recycles-72000-contaminated-single-use-plastic-bottles-in-a-world-first-move-as-new-technology-targets-petri-dishes-and-pipette-tips/articleshow/133452452.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scotland-recycles-72000-contaminated-single-use-plastic-bottles-in-a-world-first-move-as-new-technology-targets-petri-dishes-and-pipette-tips/articleshow/133452452.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T11:19:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133452732,imgsize-1538577.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian family found 102 venomous snakes hiding beneath a backyard mulch pile]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133452178.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable event in Sydney, a family found themselves in a shocking snake situation, uncovering over 40 red-bellied black snakes buried in their yard's mulch pile. After capturing these venomous reptiles, the situation escalated dramatically with adult females giving birth, leading to a total haul of 102 snakes, including 97 hatchlings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-family-noticed-snakes-disappearing-into-a-backyard-mulch-pile-snake-catchers-found-102-venomous-snakes-underneath/articleshow/133452178.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-family-noticed-snakes-disappearing-into-a-backyard-mulch-pile-snake-catchers-found-102-venomous-snakes-underneath/articleshow/133452178.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133452634,imgsize-616496.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[20-year-old student finds 1,200-year-old gold just 90 minutes into her first archaeology dig]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133451395.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an exciting turn of events, an American archaeology student has stumbled upon a ninth-century gold artifact in Northumberland during her very first excavation. This intricately designed piece, likely serving a ceremonial purpose, was found close to Dere Street, linking it to the historical narratives of Roman and early medieval Britain.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-20-year-old-archaeology-student-found-gold-just-90-minutes-into-her-first-dig-the-1200-year-old-discovery-is-raising-new-questions-about-medieval-britain/articleshow/133451395.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-20-year-old-archaeology-student-found-gold-just-90-m